00:09:25.040 --> 00:09:29.880
discussion we opened with consider a typical marina remediation project on the British Columbia

00:09:29.880 --> 00:09:35.180
coast. You arrive to find that historical dock replacements have left a measurable halo of

00:09:35.180 --> 00:09:41.160
fragmented EPS foam along the inner title and shallow subtitle zones. Phase 2 sampling reveals

00:09:41.160 --> 00:09:47.160
elevated microplastic particle counts and sorbbed PAHs that exceed British Columbia's CSR,

00:09:47.700 --> 00:09:52.500
schedule 6 sediment quality guidelines, yet laboratory reports return non-detect for

00:09:52.500 --> 00:09:58.760
parent styrene monomer. The regulatory lens continues to treat EPS primarily as physical litter

00:09:58.760 --> 00:10:03.420
under the Environmental Management Act, but experienced practitioners understand the material

00:10:03.420 --> 00:10:09.360
functions as both a vector for hydrophobic organics and a long term secondary source term that

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:14.560
must be characterized separately from traditional contaminant plumes. In the field, the defensible

00:10:14.560 --> 00:10:21.660
approach pairs a 500 micrometer newston net transect with FTIR or ramen spectroscopy performed on

00:10:21.660 --> 00:10:27.540
sieved fractions. This distinguishes adsorbed contaminant load from any inherent polymer load

00:10:27.540 --> 00:10:32.120
and supports robust mass balance calculations that regulators respect.

00:10:32.720 --> 00:10:38.580
The 20-year consultant also recognizes that EPS fragmentation rates accelerate dramatically

00:10:38.580 --> 00:10:44.320
once cumulative UV and mechanical abrasion exceed site-specific exposure thresholds dictated

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:49.860
by local wave climate and float maintenance history. That variable is rarely captured in generic

00:10:49.860 --> 00:10:54.700
marine litter guidance yet proves critical when negotiating cost allocation among responsible

00:10:54.700 --> 00:11:00.280
parties. Regulators are now routinely accepting source control plans that explicitly incorporate

00:11:00.280 --> 00:11:05.540
the new free provincial drop-off programs as evidence of due diligence. This can materially

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:10.560
shift residual liability from perpetual sediment management toward education, stewardship,

00:11:11.140 --> 00:11:17.560
and finite source removal. The single largest mistake remains treating EPS as inert trash within

00:11:17.560 --> 00:11:22.800
the risk assessment. The remedy is to add a dedicated microplastic transport module to the

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:28.860
conceptual site model, budget for polymer-specific analytics upfront, and reference the free drop-off

00:11:28.860 --> 00:11:33.920
program in every 2026 waste management and remedial action plan for coastal British Columbia

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:39.460
clients. Looking ahead at the calendar, April 22 to 24 marks the close of the Federal Impact

